note 2026-11-09T13:50:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** migration reset is per record, not per definition (narrows the
    user's migration Q1 A).

    **Why:** resetting records that still decode loses data for no safety gain; audit M2 Q18,
    `5ccc6944`, OD54 (8).

    **Reverse:** reset every record of the definition when any is incompatible.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:51:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** any structural Schema change to a stored field resets the
    record, even a harmless validation change (Q19).

    **Why:** a fixed rule `flow explain --since` can list before a deploy; OD54 (9).

    **Reverse:** reset only when the old value fails to decode.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore, @spec.Codec.
note 2026-11-09T13:52:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** the price of the rule above, said fully: an offline app loses
    saved drafts when any stored field's Schema changes, and changing a computed initial value
    resets too, until computed fields are derived on restore.

    **Why:** the cost of an automatic reset without migration functions.

    **Reverse:** a decode-based reset.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:53:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** a dropped field is applied at that release's boot, rewriting
    the records holding it (Q20), a bounded exception to D111.

    **Why:** a later re-add starts empty instead of resurrecting old data; OD54 (10).

    **Reverse:** keep D111 strict and accept resurrection.

    **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:54:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):**

    - a new identity gets its own lane (Q17);
    - the old identity's in-flight write is kept, blocks nothing, is reported at every boot, and
      ends only by its own answer;
    - `forget` does not release it.

    **Why:** a lane is (identity, contract, key); OD54 (7).

    **Reverse:** needs a new word (an identity route), the user's API call.

    **Governs:** @spec.WriteLanes, @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:55:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** the repair bound resets at `RepairOverdue`: 3 asks, then
    `RepairOverdue`, then the count starts again.

    **Why:** a doubt on a long-open screen is never stranded; stage A close-out B1, `d3d89576`.

    **Reverse:** one rule.

    **Governs:** @plan.EntityDomains.
note 2026-11-09T13:56:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** two write operations on one contract stay illegal
    (`SharedContract`, a `flow check` error).

    **Why:** the design forbids them (F2); B2.

    **Reverse:** allowing them reverses F2 and needs design work.

    **Governs:** @spec.Compile, @spec.StaticCli.
note 2026-11-09T13:57:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** entities' internal rules under `guarded` (OD52 (1), (6), (9),
    (10), (14)): a guarded doubt ends only on proof; the record queue is released once the forced
    repair settles; `Released` frees a never-re-sent unknown's queue entry; U10's later success is
    by landing order; no `allOrNothing`.

    **Why:** a doubt ends only on proof and one actor's hold blocks no other.

    **Reverse:** one rule each in rules 30 and 32.

    **Governs:** @plan.EntityDomains.
note 2026-11-09T13:58:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** streams calls (OD53): `emit.fail(e, key)` on `Feed.multiplex`;
    a key change empties a `fills` field in the same turn (`FillsOtherKey`); a session's select runs
    every committed turn; default backoff 500 ms x 2^n, jittered, capped at 30 s; 256 bookmarks per
    operation; T1 wins over T5 on Waiting; `dropAt` set on leaving Live or Repairing;
    `Feed.callback`'s 1,024 bound counts the queue only; `SelectedNoKey`.

    **Why:** OD53, audits S1, S1b.

    **Reverse:** one rule or constant each.

    **Governs:** @plan.Operations.
note 2026-11-09T13:59:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** rounds 15, 15b and area H calls (OD50, OD51): `cancelAll`
    interrupts a head on the wire and delivers the queue first, the hold-leaving head last; rule
    15's cancel exemption dropped; `forget` removes the record and a held lane stays unbound and
    reported; an Effect default is a construction error; R2, R6, R7, R8, R10 and M2 as in
